{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Why a Phone Interview?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with Will, Going to and the Present Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use different tenses to talk about the future. Each of them has their own use. It is important to understand the difference between each structure. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about <span class=\"underline\">things that are not decided</span> or when you <span class=\"underline\">make a decision at the moment of speaking</span> for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.<br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'll</span> have to prepare better answers for my next interview. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask or talk about <span class=\"underline\">intentions</span>, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to.<br>For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I know <span class=\"strong\">I'm going to</span> get nervous and lose control."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are <span class=\"underline\">arranged</span>, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.<br>For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'm calling</span> her next week to ask for a follow-up. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to practice for the interview."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm having an interview tomorrow at 3 p.m."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll call you later so we can practice! "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for information about the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tenses:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future Continuous</span> <br> <br>  will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future - the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be thinking</span> about what to say all week. </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be practicing</span> for the interview this time tomorrow. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future Perfect </span> <br><br> will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>to talk about something that will be complete by a certain time in the future </li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">By the end of the month, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have had</span> four different interviews. </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ll have answered</span> all the questions by the end of the interview. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to plagiarize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to copy another person's work without giving them credit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, once they asked me how I would deal with a journalist whom I suspected was plagiarising."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about job interviews. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "plagiarism"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the copying another person's work without giving them credit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You could try to find proof of plagiarism before you say anything."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "straightforward"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "clear; easy to follow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Questions about my experiences or education are fairly straightforward."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hypothetical"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "imaginary; something that could happen in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a hard time when they describe a hypothetical situation and ask me how I would react."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to suspect"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think; to imagine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, once they asked me how I would deal with a journalist whom I suspected was plagiarising. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le13ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a hypothetical problem you might have in a workplace."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what you would do with a partner. Give each other ideas about how to deal with it.